No lucky finds early on. I cleared out the gnomish mines and there was a
co-aligned alter on the mall level. Hurray. I blessed my luckstone and max'ed
my luck. My goddess gave my the Vorpal Blade. At this point I hadn't found
anything useful except a unicorn horn. 

Back in the Dungeons of Doom, I came across a magic lamp. I tried wishing for
a blessed figurine of a archon. The archon drops a longsword name Demonbane.
The archon drops some other junk. No reflection? My new pet did have a shield
which I never got until it died. I thought it must have been cursed, but it
wasn't. 
  Anyone know why the archon kept the shield? 
The archon was slightly amusing, but on one level, I let it get in the
room of another co-aligned preist. No more co-aligned priest. The archon 
was finally killed by a blue jelly. What a wimpy way to go.

When i found a wand of polymorph, it was time to polypile. Wands are useless
to polypile. They get destroyed too easily and you never get anything good.
  Is it a good idea to zap you wands down to (3) before polypiling? If a 
  wand of light(15) get polymorphed into something with a lower max, is it
  destroyed?
I like polypiling rings, tools, armor. All my excess scrolls and potions get
cancelled. Water gets turned into holy and unholy water. The best tools to get
are magic markers and a tinning kit which is promptly blessed. As a low level
character my favorite combination is a blessed unicorn horn and blessed 
tinning kit. I will wish for them if I find a wand of wishing before I have
them.

With a blessed unicorn horn, when you are weak from hunger, if you keep
applying it, eventually, your strength will be restored. When you eat something
and are no longer weak, your strength goes up by 1. Therefore a blessed unicorn
horn provides infinite gain strength. Coupled with a tinning kit so you can
tin every monster you kill, your strength goes to 18 quickly. Its best to stay
constantly hungry, and tins of monster meat take you from weak to hungry.

Polypiling armor will get you everything but gray dragon scale mail. I take 
all uncursed armor I have come across and sort it into 2 polypiles. In one
pile goes anything with +1 or better. The other is all +0 stuff. Cursed armor
gets cancelled and into the +0 pile. The +1 pile sometimes yields useful armor,
but also helps identify certain items. Put on a +1 helm of brilliance or
gauntlets of dexterity and they are identified. From the other pile you will
eventually get your boots of speed, cloak of displacement, shield of 
reflection, etc. I always keep spare good armor in a box in case my
original armor is damaged/destroyed.

Boxes and bags are great items for storing things. Monsters can pick up wands
and zap them at you, but if the come across a sack with 50 wands, they can't
open it up and take the wands. Dev team, you might want to do something about
this. Anyway, I always put things that are too dangerous for monsters in
designated boxes. That includes wands, extra named weapons, gold, gems, food.

The Tourist quest was too easy. Maybe it was the Vorpal Sword. I just had
to wait until I cut off the Master Thief's head. The Platinum Yendorian
Express Card is a great item!!! Infinite charging, ESP, Magic Resistance. The
timeout is less then 1000 turns.
  Can other classes wish for this quest item?
I used the cursed Bell of Opening to max my level. I got bored at 300 HP.

From here, i just had to go get the amulet and get out. My AC was below -40,
so nothing ever hurt me. I noticed a lot of posts complaining about how long
it takes to get back out. They obviously did not prepare things correctly. 
BEFORE I GOT THE AMULET, on every level, especially the maze levels, I do
two things. 1) Magic mapping via a blessed spellbook. 2) I create a direct
path between the stairs. You know all those wands of digging you have.
Use them. (I could recharge them with the Card, it was great). When I walked
back up, it took me 45 minutes. Each level took 2 shift-direction keys and I
was at the up stairs. The most time came from repeatedly killing the wizard.
I had a collection of tins of Wizard of Yendor meat. It was up to 9. Too bad
he doesn't leave a corpse more often.

I never did find Wally World.

